    <DAType id="PulseConfig" desc="Pulse configuration type is used to configure the output pulse generated with a command">
      <BDA name="cmdQual" bType="Enum" type="OutputSignalKind" desc="pulse | persistent: Defines if the control output is a pulse output or if it is a persistent output. If it is set to pulse, then the duration of the pulse shall be defined with the identifiers onDur, offDur and numPls. If it is set to persistent, the deactivation of the output pulse is a local issue determined in the server; as an example, when a switch controlled by this control output has reached the end position, the local control logic in the in the device implementing the server will deactivate the output." />
      <BDA name="onDur" bType="INT32U" desc="Duration of the pulse" />
      <BDA name="offDur" bType="INT32U" desc="Duration between two pulses" />
      <BDA name="numPls" bType="INT32U" desc="Number of pulses that are generated" />
    </DAType>
